            <ArticleTitle>The glycoprotein IIb/IIIa platelet receptor blocker tirofiban, but not heparin, counteracts platelet aggregation in unstable angina pectoris.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>938-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this study, despite concomitant aspirin treatment, tirofiban, but not heparin, reduced platelet aggregation in patients with acute myocardial ischemia. Platelet aggregation was determined with 2 independent methods, filtragometry and whole blood aggregometry.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
